puter & Web Support\nBuilding, Health & Safety\nFaculty Resources\nDepartmental Visitors\nRelocation\nLogos & Templates\nNews\nEvents\nUC Santa Barbara \\ The Robert Mehrabian College of Engineering\nSearch form\nSearch this site\nDepartment Resources\nProspective Graduate Students\nChemical Engineering - UC Santa Barbara\nAbout\nResearch\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nPeople\nResources\nNews\nEvents\nTuition and Financial Support\nGraduate Fees & Costs\nUCSB Graduate Division: Financial Support - Information about tuition, fees, and financial planning specifically for graduate students\nUCSB Office of the Registrar - Policies and procedures for tuition and fees payment\nSupport for Your Graduate Education\nIt is a policy of this department that all Ph.D. students who are within normative time, with an overall GPA above 3.0, and are making acceptable progress towards dissertation completion will receive stipend and fee payments. Stipend and fee payments for students enrolled after their fifth year of residence are not guaranteed, this is left up to the research advisor\u2019s discretion. Except under extraordinary circumstances, no student will be supported after six years of residence. All Ph.D. students receive the same level of stipend support.\nFELLOWSHIPS\nStudents who are supported by academically competitive fellowships including University Central Fellowships will receive a slightly higher stipend during the period that they are receiving fellowship support. Fellowships includes health insurance and non-resident tuition (if applicable)\nGRADUATE STUDENT RESEARCH (GSR) POSITIONS\nGraduate Student Researchers are employed and are paid monthly. This employment includes health insurance and nonresident tuition (if applicable).\nTEACHING ASSISTANTSHIPS (TA-SHIPS)\nTeaching Assistants are employed and are paid monthly. This employment includes health insurance and nonresident tuition (if applicable). Ph.D. students are required to TA at least one quarter of their second, third and fourth academic years. Assignments are made by the department.\nNeed-based Financial Aid\nNeed-based aid is only available for domestic students. To apply for aid, a Free Application for Student Aid (FAFSA) must be submitted separately. More information is available through the UCSB Financial Aid Office.\nFees Information\nConsult the Graduate Division website for more information on Graduate Student Fees and Fee Remission. The UCSB Office of the Registrar lists a summary of quarterly fees and expenses. Links: Graduate Division and Registrar\u2019s Office.\nGraduate\nAdmissions\nPhD Requirements\nCourses\nTuition & Financial Support\nAwards & Achievements\nStudent Resources\nStudent Calendar\nGraduate Student Symposium\nGraduate Student Association\nDepartment of\nCHEMICAL ENGINEERING\nEngineering II Building\nUniversity of California, Santa Barbara\nSanta Barbara, CA 93106-5080\n805.893.3412\nUCSB Chemical Engineering Facebook\nUCSB Chemical Engineering Twitter\nDirectory\nGiving\nUndergraduate Program\nGraduate Program\nPrivacy\nTerms of Use\nWeb Design Feedback\nWeb Content Feedback\nCopyright \u00a9 2020 The Regents of the University of California, All Rights Reserved.", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.chemengr.ucsb.edu/graduate/admissions/tuition-and-financial-support#main-content"], ["About", "https://www.chemengr.ucsb.edu/about"], ["Location", "https://www.chemengr.ucsb.edu/about/location"], ["Rankings and Awards", "https://www.chemengr.ucsb.edu/about/rankings-awards"], ["External Advisory Board", "https://www.chemengr.ucsb.edu/about/external-advisory-board"], ["Newsletters", "https://www.chemengr.ucsb.edu/about/newsletters"], ["Giving", "https://www.chemengr.ucsb.edu/about/giving"], ["Alumni", "https://www.chemengr.ucsb.edu/alumni"], ["Employment Opportunities", "https://www.chemengr.ucsb.edu/about/employmentopportunities"], ["Mellichamp Emerging Leader Lectures", "https://www.chemengr.ucsb.edu/duncan-suzanne-mellichamp-emerging-